his sequence reduces my hand from 13 cards to 3 cards (9, J, A), putting tremendous pressure on the Landlord and setting up a potential win or assist for my teammate. The certainty of clearing 10 cards outweighs the marginal benefit of trying to save the 2 for the endgame.\n\nReason: To preserve and play the 9-card straight (4-Q), which constitutes the bulk of my hand, I must secure the lead. Playing the ♣2 guarantees the lead, allowing me to play the straight on the next turn and reduce my hand count to 3 singles. Risking the loss of initiative by playing a smaller card is too dangerous given the specialized nature of my hand.\n\nAnswer: {"cards": ["♣2"]}'}
